WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.601
-Our next guest is
a talented actress

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.870
who wrote, produced and, stars
in "Shelter in Solitude",

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.739
which will be in theaters
October 6th.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.809
Let's take a look.
-Normally,

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.514
the way a conversation goes
is, "Do you have children?

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.350
You have kids?"
"No. Do you, Valerie?"

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.754
"No, I don't, Jackson."
"Why don't you, Valerie?"

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:23.957
"Oh, because...

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.662
I never married."

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:34.334
-Why not?

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.275
-I don't know.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:46.079
My daddy always said it was
'cause I intimidated the boys

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:48.714
'cause I had
unearned effervescence.

00:00:48.714 --> 00:00:51.951
-Please welcome to the show,
Siobhan Fallon Hogan.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:54.954
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.954 --> 00:01:05.097 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.766
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.135
-I am thrilled to be here, Seth.
I'm thrilled.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.804
-So you used to work
in this building

00:01:10.804 --> 00:01:12.104
at a "Saturday Night Live".

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:14.006
Have you been back since then?
-I just went over there,

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:15.375
and I said,
"Does anybody remember me?"

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.576
And they said,
"What year are you here?"

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:22.048
I said, "20- and, uh,
20- and -2000 years ago."

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.816
-[ Laughs ]
And they hate doing the math.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.818
-They're like, "Who are ya?"
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:28.121
-I actually said, "1902",
but I forgot my joke.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.989
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.092
-So now you --
you wrote, you produced,

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.459
and you starred in this movie.
-Yes.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:34.927
-I know how hard it can be

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.662
to make an independent film
like this.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:39.132
How long did it take the process
from start to finish?

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.567
-Start to finish? Okay.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.101
I was laying in bed one night
in the middle of the night.

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:43.269
I had written
a movie called "Rushed",

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.171
which came out two years ago,

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.306
and I said I'm taking a break
because I'm elderly.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.909
And so, I -- then this idea
came to me

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:50.910
in the middle of the night.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.845
My dad had been an attorney --

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.548
I'm from five kids,
I'm the second of five --

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.316
and he used to tell us
about these prisoners,

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.552
that he represented,
at our -- at our kitchen table.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.888
And I'd be kind of, like,
terrified but really fascinated.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:03.989
And so, he also wanted me
to be a country

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:05.391
[Voice raises] singer,

00:02:05.391 --> 00:02:07.026
[Normal voice]
but I didn't have the voice.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.095
-Oh, I thought the way
you said "singer" was beautiful.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.095
-You like that?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:10.095 --> 00:02:12.064
-I'm affected. So... Okay.

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:14.533
So, I have red nails.
I got it going on for the show.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.568
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-So, okay...

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.136
So anyway, so this idea
came to me

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.270
in the middle of the night,
and I said,

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.575
"What if a prisoner
has 10 days left to live

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:26.478
and a washed up country singer
becomes his guard?"

00:02:26.478 --> 00:02:28.214
And so, that's where
the idea came from.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.882
And I said, "Wait a minute,
I got to have Robert Patrick

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.550
in there", you know,
from "The Terminator".

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.119
He's fabulous, and he played
my husband in "Rushed".

00:02:34.119 --> 00:02:36.355
I was like,
"We need a hard ass warden."

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.091
And so --
I wasn't supposed to swear.

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:39.192
Sorry.
-That's okay.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.961
-And so, anyway,
that's where it came from.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.596
And then I wrote it
in three weeks,

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:45.431
and we filmed it in 16 days.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.367
-That's incredible.
That is not a lot of time.

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.236
-No.
-You produced it

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.906
with your husband, but you also
involved your children.

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.240
-Yes. My son is a producer.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.841
He's a music supervisor,
which, by the way,

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.176
he would freak out
about your band.

00:02:57.176 --> 00:02:58.310
I'm, like, back there rocking.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:00.112
I'm like,
he loves music so much.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:02.381
And he hooked me up
with Justin Biltonen

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:04.584
from 3 Doors Down
for country fans.

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:07.419
I sang with him last Tuesday
in Nashville.

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:08.954
-Look at you.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:11.724
-Who's not a country singer?
-Come on.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.426
I was on a rooftop singing --

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:15.461
He wrote this song
"Heartache Rodeo".

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.229
-Okay. Were other people
on the rooftop?

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.365
Or was that something
you chose to do? Yeah.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.133
-Well, my son booked it all.
-Oh, great.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.901
-And then my daughter, Sinead,
I gotta mention her --

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.604
I'll get punched in the face
when I get home --

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.240
she -- she was the production
designer.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.874
And then my daughter,
Bernadette, she's a journalist.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:31.110
So, she would help me the copy.
Anyway, we're all involved.

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.413
Even the dog. It's called
Trudy Ville, the town.

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:38.884
So we're all in on it.
And my son plays Chris, the cop.

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:40.987
And, you know,
it was an insane asylum

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.489
because I'm not nocturnal.
-Yeah.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.325
-And so, that's why,
like, whatever.

00:03:46.325 --> 00:03:49.929
But anyway,
I'd say there's rules.

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.897
Okay? We have to have rules.
No one listens to me.

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:54.367
You know, we're an Irish family.
It's ridiculous.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.469
And so, I said,
"Do not wake me up.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.571
We're filming this movie.
I'm the producer.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.839
I have to, like,
get the porta potty --"

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.007
-You need your sleep, yeah.
-Yeah, I gotta make sure

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.075
the porta potties are clean.

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:03.675
My husband's getting food
for the crew,

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:05.311
and my son knock on the door
at 2:00 in the morning,

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.880
"Um, can I talk to you
about that scene?"

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.615
I go, "I thought --
I thought we had a rule."

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.350
And he's like, "I'm sorry,

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.786
but I think we should say,
'Skedaddle, Valerie.'

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.021
And then you should say,
'Skedaddle' back."

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:16.522
And I go, "That's funny.
Come in."

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.558
So -- So I look terrible
in the movie,

00:04:19.558 --> 00:04:21.394
but I'm supposed to be
washed up, so it doesn't matter.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:22.694
-Oh, yeah. There you go.
That's very smart.

00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:24.497
-I mean -- I mean,
what is happening under my eyes?

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.998
I don't know.
-You, like, save money

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:28.133
on a makeup person
when you just stay up all night.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.436
-Completely. And I was --
And I was also a cougar wannabe.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:31.570
-Oh, yeah?
-Yeah, and so,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.905
I'm supposed to try
to have an affair --

00:04:32.905 --> 00:04:35.875
well, try is --
heavy on the try --

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.077
with this Michael Oberholtzer,
who's a fabulous actor.

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:41.213
But I want to give a massive,
massive shout out.

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:44.617
Peter Macon, the guy
who plays the actor

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.753
who plays the prisoner --
-Yeah, the death row inmate.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:49.688
-...it was an Oscar worthy
performance.

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:51.057
-That's fantastic.
You also --

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.158
I know you filmed it
in Syracuse,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:53.358
which is where you're from.

00:04:53.358 --> 00:04:55.094
Did you actually
cast some locals

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.129
that you knew back in the day?
-Oh, I did. I --

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.731
Matter of fact --
So the bar scenes,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:00.299
which it didn't rain
the whole time,

00:05:00.299 --> 00:05:03.102
which is really unusual
for Syracuse,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:05.537
and so, the only days
it rained was the bar.

00:05:05.537 --> 00:05:07.073
And guess how I got
all my extras?

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:12.011
-How? Free beer?
-Thanks for asking.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:15.280
Close, I said to the class
of '79,

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.116
which not to date myself,

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:20.285
I said to my class, "Whoever
wants to be an extra can come

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:21.787
and be in the bar scene."

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.389
So that's my entire class
from '79.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:24.890
-Oh, my God.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.525
-That's fantastic.
They all showed up for you?

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:27.860
-They all showed.
People flew in from all over.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.428
And it's literally like,
I go to Nashville,

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.430
they come there,
I'm like, I have an entour--

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.799
Like, when I was on "SNL",
I remember MC Hammer came

00:05:33.799 --> 00:05:36.001
and he had, like, an entourage.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.001 --> 00:05:37.537
-And now I have one.
-It just took you

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.938
a little bit longer
to reach your Hammer era.

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:42.041
-Yeah.
Guess what else I have?

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:44.177
-What?
-So...

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.644
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.644 --> 00:05:48.214
I probably shouldn't say this.
-You have the energy

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.915
of someone who probably
shouldn't say it.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.417
-Should I not?
-Say it.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.519
-I have a perv. I have a perv.

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.521
Somebody called me and, like,
did weird breathing.

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:57.423
-You have your own perv?
-And I go, "I made it."

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:01.026
-Oh, my God.
Siobhan, we're so --

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:03.228
we're so happy for you.
-Yes.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:04.797
I went over. I went o--
Matter of fact,

00:06:04.797 --> 00:06:06.231
I went over
to "Saturday Night Live".

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.634
You know, I had PTSD
when I came 'cause, you know...

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.802
-Yeah.
-Well, you know, I left

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:13.005
for "artistic differences" --
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.575
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:17.076
-...in '92.

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:19.778
Anyway, so I went over,
and I went on the stage,

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.513
and the guys were so nice.

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:24.316
And I said, "Live from New York,
it's Wednesday night.

00:06:24.316 --> 00:06:25.818
I'm on Seth Meyers show."

00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.586
-Well, there you go.
And here you are.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.255
And congratulations
on the movie.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:30.956
Everybody, check it out.
It's an independent film.

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.692
These are the kind of movies
we need to go see.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:35.661
You guys,
that is Siobhan Fallon Hogan.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:38.331
"Shelter in Solitude"
in theaters October 6th.

00:06:38.331 --> 00:06:39.532
Go see it and stick around.

00:06:39.532 --> 00:06:41.067
We'll be right back
with music from Jungle.

